WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.190
Hi, I'm Scupper!

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.488
Unzip needs room for the archive and every file at once.

00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:07.887
This tool only needs room for the files.

00:00:09.225 --> 00:00:13.221
A zip compresses each entry alone and keeps its index at the end.

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:15.987
So extract the last entries, then shorten the file.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.946
Before anything is cut, the index at the end of the archive

00:00:22.946 --> 00:00:24.782
is copied to a small side file.

00:00:25.202 --> 00:00:28.363
Then it takes entries from the end, as many as fit in

00:00:28.363 --> 00:00:30.471
the free space, and extracts them in parallel.

00:00:30.891 --> 00:00:34.093
Once the files are flushed to disk, the journal records how long

00:00:34.093 --> 00:00:35.427
the archive should now be.

00:00:35.847 --> 00:00:37.643
Only then is the archive truncated.

00:00:37.643 --> 00:00:40.635
The space it gives back pays for the next batch.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.291
Truncation works everywhere, but it frees an entry only once all

00:00:45.291 --> 00:00:46.433
of it is out.

00:00:46.853 --> 00:00:50.345
For a file bigger than the free space, it punches holes behind

00:00:50.345 --> 00:00:51.509
each flushed step instead.

00:00:53.258 --> 00:00:56.908
In the project's animation, the archive loses blocks from its end.

00:00:57.328 --> 00:00:59.647
The disk never has to hold both at full size.

00:01:01.192 --> 00:01:02.400
And if it dies halfway?

00:01:03.503 --> 00:01:06.261
The archive is only ever cut back to the last commit.

00:01:06.681 --> 00:01:09.148
Running it again redoes one batch and finishes.

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:12.344
Or restore turns what is left back into a normal zip.

00:01:13.758 --> 00:01:17.255
On a disk too small for unzip, it ran the disk nearly

00:01:17.255 --> 00:01:19.004
full and finished, every file intact.

00:01:20.725 --> 00:01:22.771
On a roomy disk it peaks like unzip.

00:01:22.771 --> 00:01:25.841
On a tight one, each batch shrinks to fit the freed space.

00:01:29.442 --> 00:01:32.846
Extract from the end, journal before every cut, and punch holes for

00:01:32.846 --> 00:01:34.548
the files that will not fit.

00:01:34.968 --> 00:01:37.078
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:37.078 --> 00:01:37.680
I'm Scupper.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:37.982
Bye!
